In article <12976@umn-cs.CS.UMN.EDU> clark@umn-cs.CS.UMN.EDU (Robert P. Clark) writes:
>
>    Does sacrificing dead monsters please or anger the gods?  Does it
>matter if the monster is edible?  What does it mean if they won't take
>the sacrifice?

The gods won't accept "stale" monsters.  (Dead monsters go stale after, what,
50 turns?)  If the gods don't want it, you probably won't want to eat it
either.  You'll want to avoid sacrificing poisonous monsters because that
makes them angry.  Other than that, I believe that the goodness of a
sacrifice varies according to the inherent food value.

